---
// /documentation/troubleshooting
// Problems listed by what the admin notices. For exact messages, see error-messages.astro.
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import ClickPath from '../../components/docs/ClickPath.astro';
---
<DocsLayout slug="troubleshooting">
  <p class="docs-lede">Find what you're seeing. If you have an exact message, search for it on the <a href="/documentation/error-messages">Error messages</a> page instead.</p>

  <h2 id="setup">During setup</h2>
  <div class="docs-table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What you see</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>The AI Assist app isn't in the App Launcher</td><td>Assign yourself AI Assist Super User in <ClickPath steps={['Setup', 'Permission Sets']} />.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>You can't open the wizard, models, tools or settings</td><td>Those tabs need AI Assist Super User. AI Assist Admin isn't enough.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>The connection test says "setup problem"</td><td>Check the Named Credential's URL, that <code>LoomConnect</code> is in Allowed Namespaces for Callouts, and that you have the provider access permission set.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>The connection test says "authentication error"</td><td>The API key is wrong. Paste it again on the External Credential's principal, with no spaces.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Your named credential isn't in the model's list</td><td>Refresh the AI Agent Models tab. Check the Named Credential saved and is enabled for callouts.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>The wizard won't activate the agent</td><td>The Review step lists what's blocking it. Most often there's no active model.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="users">When users start chatting</h2>
  <div class="docs-table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What you see</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>The chat window isn't on the page</td><td>Check the record page was activated for the user's app and profile, or that the utility item was saved.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"AI Assist has not been set up for your user"</td><td>No usage policy applies. Make an active policy the default on the AI Policies tab.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>"No AI agent is available for this record"</td><td>Check the agent is active and lists this object on its Basics step.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Messages fail for users but work for you</td><td>Users are missing the provider access permission set, so they can't use the key.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Answers leave out information</td><td>The user can't see that data, or the agent has no data source for it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Users hit limits too often</td><td>Check the Hit a Limit list view, then raise limits on the policy or the agent.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="help">Still stuck</h2>
  <p>Raise a request on the <a href="/support">support page</a>. Include the exact message, the time it happened and any matching entry from the AI Platform Log tab. Never send your API key.</p>
</DocsLayout>
